					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13909309#post-4842443</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13909309/scp-5587#post-4842443</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 11 Dec 2020 17:52:14 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>FinlandSite_Helsinki</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>6949371</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This SCP reminds me of the classic first SCPs of the site, more of an informational page than a thrilling story that most SCPs today must have to succeed. I think this is honestly by the book, it has all the detail we need, it’s not necessarily confusing, and it has almost zero grammatical or spelling errors which means the author put some work into making sure this is perfect. While I didn’t find this SCP particularly exciting it’s what the site was built on and feels more like an actual research log than a story that seems more like a tale which is what most current SCPs are like nowadays. Good work though! +1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
